title: Psalms 36–37: The Fountain of Life, and Fret Not Thyself
description: Psalms 36-37 in the King James Bible: no fear of God before his eyes, the fountain of life and in thy light shall we see light, fret not thyself because of evildoers and the gratitude that drives out anxiety, trust in the LORD and do good, salt and light, and the desires of thine heart, from the Psalms series studies.
output: lessons/bible/psalms-36-37.html
context: yes

